Well, this is the first time I got anywhere: I killed Vlad, had the
bell and the candlabra, and I was heading back for some candles when...

I decided to eat an Orange that fell off a tree in Gnometown and
chocked to death.  I guess "slow digestion" really means slow
digestion! =P

I was a Gnomish Wizard XL20, I had my stats maxed and a -30AC

I had a very lucky game find two bags of holding off bones files early
on, 5 magic markers here and there,  amulet of reflection in Sokoban
and the usual luckstone.  The early protection run was easy because
Minetown wasn't very deep and I managed to raise a bunch of gold
cleaning out shops.  I wrote two blessed scrolls of charging and two
blessed scrolls of genocide when I found the markers.

I was a shamless exploiter genociding all L and all H (I didn't realize
this included hobbits and Dwaves, but was lucky it didn't include
Gnomes lol).  I played around with polypiling but the only useful
things I got out of that were a few cans of grease and a ring of
levitation (I'm not complaining).  I played around with alchemy to max
all my stats (not that they were far from maxed by the time I did
this).

I wished for a helm of brilliance, gauntlets of dexterity, a ring of
slow digestion and silver dragon scalemail.

I was very well stocked with stuff.  I guess I had never got this far
before.  I really wasn't breaking a sweat doing much of anything.  It's
good to be a Wizard!

I did a lot of dumb things including losing my protection about 3 times
by praying at the wrong time and I taking a little swim a few time
while carrying my bags of holding (before I had greased them), but
recovery wasn't hard.  The money from Fort Ludos payed for plenty of
more protection and most of my good spell books, scrolls and potions
were in tact.

Dying was actually very funny.  I was beginning to care less and less
about the game other than that I might actually ascend.  Now I'm not
sure if I care whether I ever do ascend or not :)

Anyway, after playing what seems like 100's of games where I didn't get
far passed either Sokoban or Gnometown, it was very nice to play this
game and see some of the things I've heard so much about!



